      "body": "<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=64010806\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=1\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=1\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=1\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 5/5</h2>\n\nThe PR appears safe to merge, with the guarded behavior and fallback paths covered by focused unit and real-QGIS rendering tests.\n\n<details><summary><h3>Summary</h3></summary>\n\n- Adds strict source-style, native-core, symbol-shape, and existing-override guards.\n- Applies the background repair after the ordinary national-boundary core repair.\n- Adds unit and real-QGIS rendering coverage for zoom interpolation, status fallback, opacity override semantics, and DPI scaling.\n- Updates the Light cartographic assessment while keeping unresolved fidelity and output-consistency work open.\n</details>\n\n<details open><summary><h3>Diagram</h3></summary>\n\n```mermaid\n%%{init: {'theme': 'neutral'}}%%\nflowchart TD\n  A[Converted Light vector renderer] --> B[Apply road-width repairs]\n  B --> C[Repair ordinary national-boundary core]\n  C --> D{Exact Light source and repaired-core guards pass?}\n  D -- No --> E[Preserve native background paint]\n  D -- Yes --> F{Eligible unmodified background symbol?}\n  F -- No --> E\n  F -- Yes --> G[Install status-aware width and opacity expressions]\n  G --> H{disputed equals false?}\n  H -- Yes --> I[Use source width and opacity by zoom]\n  H -- No --> J[Use captured native width and opacity]\n  I --> K[Install renderer on background layer]\n  J --> K\n  E --> K\n```\n</details>\n\n<sub>Reviews (1) \u00b7 Last reviewed commit: [\"docs: record scoped national-background ...\"](https://github.com/ebelo/qfit/commit/cc32c99ee217fb87632fd1bd8e2d3dbff4ae8fe8)</sub>",
